      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Playing basic Swamp instead of Gloomlake Verge on turn 1 is slightly suboptimal. Gloomlake Verge can only tap for B unconditionally (without controlling an Island or Swamp). By playing Gloomlake Verge first, it taps for B immediately. Then on turn 2, playing Watery Grave (which is an Island and Swamp) would enable Gloomlake Verge to also tap for U. If instead you play Swamp turn 1 and Gloomlake Verge turn 2, you get the same result — Gloomlake Verge sees the Swamp and can tap for both colors. So functionally, the sequencing doesn't matter much for turns 1-2. However, playing Gloomlake Verge first preserves more flexibility: if you draw another non-basic land that needs basics, having the basic Swamp still in hand is better. Playing the Verge first is marginally better since it keeps the basic Swamp available for future land drops where a basic might matter (e.g., against opposing effects that care about basics, or if you need to play a land that enters tapped unless you control a basic). This is a very small sequencing error.",
