      "description": "Casting Sunpearl Kirin on turn 2 main phase is suboptimal for several reasons. First, the player should play Hallowed Fountain from hand before casting spells to have more mana available in future turns and avoid missing a land drop. Second, Sunpearl Kirin has flash, meaning it could be held up and cast at end of opponent's turn to preserve information and flexibility. Third, casting it now with no other nonland permanents worth bouncing means the ETB trigger returns nothing, and playing it pre-combat when holding Kaito (which has ninjutsu) means the Kirin could have been used as an unblocked attacker to ninjutsu Kaito in. Playing Grim Bauble first would also be reasonable as it provides a target for Sunpearl Kirin's bounce ability later.",
